<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vima Takto</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vima Takto was a Kushan emperor of the late 1st century CE, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kujula-kadphises">Kujula Kadphises</a> and grandfather of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanishka">Kanishka</a>. Long known only from anonymous coins issued in the name of Soter Megas, the Great Saviour, he was identified by name when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabatak-inscription">Rabatak inscription</a> was found in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> in 1993. He expanded Kushan rule into north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vima-takto.jpg" alt="Vima Takto" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Per Honor et Gloria · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Kushan_King_Vima_Takto.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
